          "why": "An exterior angle equals the sum of the two opposite interior angles.",
          "sol": "Step 1: Use the exterior angle rule.\nStep 2: Exterior angle = 38° + 72°.\nStep 3: Exterior angle = 110°.",
          "hint": "Add the two opposite interior angles.",
          "subject": "math",
          "chapter": "geometry",
          "topic": "Exterior Angle of a Triangle",
          "conceptId": "math_geometry_exterior_angle_of_a_triangle",
