          "why": "Cross multiplication removes ratios and forms a solvable equation",
          "sol": "Step 1: Write proportion 6/9 = x/27\nStep 2: Cross multiply → 6 × 27 = 9x\nStep 3: Compute 162 = 9x\nStep 4: Divide both sides by 9\nStep 5: Solve for x",
          "hint": "cross multiplication",
          "subject": "math",
          "chapter": "ratio",
          "topic": "Proportion",
          "conceptId": "math_ratio_proportion",
          "skillId": "math_ratio",
          "subskillId": "math_ratio_q1"
