          "why": "The fraction has favourable outcomes on top and total outcomes below.",
          "sol": "Step 1: Favourable outcomes = 1.\nStep 2: Total outcomes = 6.\nStep 3: Therefore P(6) = 1/6.",
          "hint": "There is one favourable outcome out of six.",
          "subject": "math",
          "chapter": "probability",
          "topic": "Writing Probability as a Fraction",
          "conceptId": "math_probability_writing_probability_as_a_fraction",
          "skillId": "math_probability",
